WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:06.700 --> 00:00:09.900
We have heard of temperatures like Zero degrees Celsius,

00:00:09.900 --> 00:00:12.920
which is the Freezing Point of Water,

00:00:13.180 --> 00:00:17.600
and 100 degrees Celsius, which is the Boiling Point of Water.

00:00:17.760 --> 00:00:21.580
Though Celsius is a more Common way to measure the temperature,

00:00:21.780 --> 00:00:26.340
Fahrenheit is also sometimes used as its unit of Measure.

00:00:26.440 --> 00:00:31.900
Zero degree Celsius is the equivalent of 32 degrees Fahrenheit.

00:00:32.060 --> 00:00:36.120
There is a particular way in which, we can convert Celsius to Fahrenheit,

00:00:36.180 --> 00:00:38.720
and vice Versa.

00:00:38.720 --> 00:00:42.260
This is the formula to convert Celsius to Fahrenheit.

00:00:42.460 --> 00:00:44.980
We multiply the temperature in Celsius,

00:00:45.040 --> 00:00:49.940
with 'nine over five' and add 32 to it.

00:00:50.080 --> 00:00:51.900
And modifying this formula,

00:00:51.900 --> 00:00:55.920
we get the conversion from Fahrenheit to Celsius.

00:00:55.960 --> 00:00:59.140
Subtract 32 from the temperature in Fahrenheit,

00:00:59.380 --> 00:01:03.760
multiply it with five and divide the entire thing by nine.

00:01:04.020 --> 00:01:08.740
So how much time do you think you'll take to convert one to another?

00:01:09.000 --> 00:01:13.620
Twelve degrees Celsius is how many degrees Fahrenheit?

00:01:13.840 --> 00:01:17.920
Or 23 degrees Fahrenheit is how many degrees Celsius?

00:01:18.180 --> 00:01:21.040
Look at it a bit practically.

00:01:21.240 --> 00:01:23.880
If somebody asks you this in real life,

00:01:23.880 --> 00:01:27.460
they are not expecting a perfect answer!

00:01:27.500 --> 00:01:30.220
What you need is an approximate value.

00:01:30.400 --> 00:01:33.720
Using these formulae will give you the perfect answer,

00:01:33.720 --> 00:01:36.500
but you'll take too long to arrive at it.

00:01:36.620 --> 00:01:41.240
So let's see a quicker way to arrive at an approximate answer.

00:01:41.400 --> 00:01:45.140
Let's say you want to convert Celsius to Fahrenheit!

00:01:45.300 --> 00:01:51.600
All we need to do is multiply the temperature in Celsius with two, and add 30 to it.

00:01:51.900 --> 00:01:54.780
That will give us the answer in Fahrenheit.

00:01:54.960 --> 00:02:00.320
Say 10 degrees celsius, we need to convert this into Fahrenheit.

00:02:00.420 --> 00:02:03.700
Multiply it with 2, and add 30.

00:02:03.940 --> 00:02:07.340
20 plus 30 is 50 degrees.

00:02:07.500 --> 00:02:09.420
10 degrees Celsius

00:02:09.420 --> 00:02:12.980
is approximately 50 degrees Fahrenheit.

00:02:12.980 --> 00:02:16.960
Multiply with 2 and add 30 to the product.

00:02:17.000 --> 00:02:19.560
17 degrees Celsius.

00:02:19.700 --> 00:02:25.640
'17 times 2' is 34 and '34 plus 30' is 64.

00:02:25.840 --> 00:02:27.800
17 degrees Celsius,

00:02:27.800 --> 00:02:30.960
is approximately 64 degrees Fahrenheit.

00:02:31.120 --> 00:02:34.300
If we do the exact Calculations using the formulae,

00:02:34.620 --> 00:02:39.480
we would have got 10 degrees Celsius as 50 degrees Fahrenheit.

00:02:39.480 --> 00:02:42.120
Yes, we were a bit fortunate here .

00:02:42.400 --> 00:02:47.420
And 17 degrees Celsius as '62 point six degrees Fahrenheit'.

00:02:47.600 --> 00:02:49.200
Almost equal.

00:02:49.380 --> 00:02:53.400
The higher the temperature, the bigger will be the difference.

00:02:53.400 --> 00:02:56.020
Say 50 degrees Celsius.

00:02:56.200 --> 00:02:57.280
'100 plus 30'

00:02:57.680 --> 00:03:00.760
is 130 degrees Fahrenheit.

00:03:00.940 --> 00:03:03.160
The exact answer is

00:03:03.160 --> 00:03:07.720
122, a difference of eight degrees Fahrenheit.

00:03:07.980 --> 00:03:11.140
And converting 100 degree Celsius To Fahrenheit,

00:03:11.380 --> 00:03:16.980
we get 230 degrees approximately, and the exact answer

00:03:16.980 --> 00:03:19.820
is 212 degrees Fahrenheit.

00:03:20.060 --> 00:03:22.160
So as the number increases,

00:03:22.200 --> 00:03:26.800
the difference or error in the answer, also increases!

00:03:27.160 --> 00:03:29.640
Does this work for negative Temperatures as well?

00:03:29.960 --> 00:03:31.460
Absolutely.

00:03:31.800 --> 00:03:34.340
'Say Minus 15 degrees Celsius'.

00:03:34.540 --> 00:03:38.080
'Minus 15' times 2 Is 'Minus 30.'

00:03:38.360 --> 00:03:41.920
And 'minus 30' plus 30 equals 0.

00:03:42.160 --> 00:03:44.320
'Minus 15 degrees Celsius'.

00:03:44.320 --> 00:03:47.640
is approximately Zero degrees Fahrenheit.

00:03:47.860 --> 00:03:51.040
The exact value comes out to be 5 degrees Fahrenheit.

00:03:51.580 --> 00:03:54.620
So to convert from Celsius to Fahrenheit,

00:03:54.760 --> 00:03:59.300
just multiply by 2 and add 30 to the product.

00:03:59.620 --> 00:04:03.340
And how do we quickly convert Fahrenheit to Celsius?

00:04:03.560 --> 00:04:07.620
Easy, we subtract 30 and then divide by 2.

00:04:07.880 --> 00:04:14.340
Take 100 degrees Fahrenheit for example, we subtract 30 and get 70.

00:04:14.400 --> 00:04:18.640
And 70 over 2 is equal to 35.

00:04:18.660 --> 00:04:20.860
100 degrees Fahrenheit is

00:04:20.940 --> 00:04:24.260
approximately equal to 35 degrees Celsius .

00:04:24.320 --> 00:04:27.400
The exact answer if you calculate is

00:04:27.460 --> 00:04:30.920
thirty seven point seven seven seven eight degrees Celsius.

00:04:31.280 --> 00:04:33.660
The difference isn't much.

00:04:33.880 --> 00:04:37.100
What about 72 degrees Fahrenheit?

00:04:37.300 --> 00:04:40.320
Subtract 30 and get 42.

00:04:40.540 --> 00:04:43.840
'42 over two' is 21.

00:04:44.060 --> 00:04:50.060
'72 degrees Fahrenheit' is approximately equal to '21 degrees Celsius.'

00:04:50.220 --> 00:04:55.060
Now let's try converting 'Minus 40 degrees Fahrenheit' to Celsius.

00:04:55.340 --> 00:04:59.000
Subtracting 30, we get 'Minus 70.'

00:04:59.200 --> 00:05:04.780
And dividing it by 2, we get 'minus 35 degrees Celsius' approximately.

00:05:04.960 --> 00:05:11.320
The exact value in these two cases is '22.222 degrees Celsius' and

00:05:11.320 --> 00:05:14.200
'minus 40 degrees Celsius'.

00:05:14.320 --> 00:05:17.400
A very small degree of error in each case.

00:05:17.500 --> 00:05:20.760
But what if you forget the ways of conversion?

00:05:20.920 --> 00:05:22.920
Remember, for the same temperature,

00:05:22.940 --> 00:05:25.540
Fahrenheit is always larger.

00:05:25.800 --> 00:05:27.260
So multiplying it with 2

00:05:27.340 --> 00:05:31.060
and adding 30 will definitely give us a larger number.

00:05:31.320 --> 00:05:33.560
To convert from Celsius To Fahrenheit,

00:05:33.700 --> 00:05:35.900
we multiply and add!

00:05:36.140 --> 00:05:38.880
And as Celsius is a smaller number,

00:05:38.980 --> 00:05:41.800
we subtract 30 and divide by 2.

00:05:42.200 --> 00:05:46.720
One good way to remember this is that 'C' comes before 'F'.

00:05:46.800 --> 00:05:48.900
So 'C' is smaller than 'F'.

